[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports say otherwise.
Read by what they show, not by subject line or intake tag, they are three problems.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`)
and the booking-v3 form is retired, so its hint won't be fixed. Neither touches the third problem.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but not done. Reports of dates that move by one day are still open, with no fix.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {problems} />

## How each report was placed

- **One report, one id.** The export pages overlap, so some reports come twice.
- **`hint`** — it came through the booking form of a booking-v3 tenant. The form tells people to
  type month first and then reads the date day first.
- **`parser`** — every other report from a day-first tenant: the shared parser swaps day and month.
- **`one-day`** — the desk read it as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`). Nothing is swapped: the
  same meeting lands a day apart for people in different places. Neither other fix touches it.
  As on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471), these stay counted where they're filed, and are counted here too.

The cause comes from the tenant (`causes.ts`, `locales.ts`), never from the intake tag. Intake
guesses from the reporter's browser, and often guesses wrong.

## Why the subject line hid them

Triage merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). The subject
does not tell these problems apart: "Wrong day on the invite" is the subject of reports in all three.
Try it in [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe): same subject, different tenant or channel, different cause.

